.TH "CSSNUMERICVALUE.SUB" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSNumericValue.sub \- CSSNumericValue: sub() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]sub()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R]
interface subtracts a supplied number from the
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
sub()
sub(number1)
sub(number1, number2)
sub(number1, number2, /* \&..., */ numberN)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]number1\f[R], \&..., \f[B]numberN\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
Either a number or a \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R], or a \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] if \f[CR]this\f[R]
and every argument share the same unit.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if an invalid type was passed to the method.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
.IP
.EX
\f[B]let\f[R] mathSum = CSS.px(23).sub(CSS.percent(4)).sub(CSS.cm(3)).sub(CSS.in(9));
\f[I]// Prints \(dqcalc(23px \- 4% \- 3cm \- 9in)\(dq\f[R]
console.log(mathSum.toString());
.EE
